{
  "schema": 1,
  "note": "The prompt glyph tables (docs/controls/prompt-glyphs.md sections 2, 3 and 5), as data. Controls owns the bindings and this map; UI draws the glyphs. The default style is NEUTRAL: our own position diamond with a letter mark for the face buttons, and plain text marks for the rest; no console maker's icon art is reproduced, and no platform's face symbols are used until Legal answers (prompt-glyphs.md rule 7). The 'family' style, which prints each family's own letters, exists in the data but is off until then. Keyboard glyphs are a keycap with the label on the player's layout (the host may replace the label with DisplayServer.keyboard_get_label_from_physical).",
  "families": ["kbd", "xbox", "ps", "switch", "deck", "generic"],
  "neutral": {
    "face": { "south": "S", "east": "E", "west": "W", "north": "N" },
    "pad": { "LT": "LT", "RT": "RT", "LB": "LB", "RB": "RB", "R3": "R3" }
  },
  "family_labels": {
